{{smaller block|That shall we come to, if we can take order that while we be here, before we go hence, our bodies, we get them ''templified'', as I may say, procure they be framed after the similitude of a Temple, this Temple in the text [John ii. 19].{{right|''Bp. Andrews'', Sermons, II. 361. (''Davies.'')}}}}

'''templin-oil''' (tem′plin-oil), ''n.'' [< ''templin'' (?) + ''oil.''] Oil of pine-cones; an oil isomeric with and very similar to oil of turpentine, obtained by distillation of the cones of ''Pinus Pumilio.''

